    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.today — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.today#\n\n- \nclassmethod Timestamp.today(*tz=None* )#\n- Return the current time in the local timezone. This differs from datetime.today() in that it can be localized to a passed timezone. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **tz** str or timezone object, default None\n    - Timezone to localize to.\n See also \n  - `datetime.datetime.today`\n  - Returns the current local date.\n  - `Timestamp.now`\n  - Returns current time with optional timezone.\n  - `Timestamp`\n  - A class representing a specific timestamp.\n Examples >>> pd.Timestamp.today() Timestamp('2020-11-16 22:37:39.969883') Analogous for `pd.NaT` :>>> pd.NaT.today() NaT",
    "markdown_length": 633,
